{
  "description": "A stout, low-slung quadrupedal creature is shown in right-facing profile standing on a small patch of dry, sandy ground with sparse tufts of grass. It has the overall build of a large tortoise with a high, domed shell, a short thick neck, a blunt reptilian head, four massive columnar legs, and a short pointed tail. The dorsal and lateral surfaces of the shell are densely covered with long, shaggy, coarse brown fur that hangs over the shell rim like a coat, while the exposed rim of the shell shows light tan to brown scutes with concentric growth lines. The head, neck, legs, and tail are covered in dry, polygonal reptilian scales in tan and brown tones, and the coloration overall is muted earthy browns and tans on an off-white background.",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "head",
      "looks_like": "large, blunt and reptilian with a tortoise-like beak, covered in large polygonal tan-brown scales, with a single dark eye with a scaly eyelid, two small nostrils at the tip of the snout, and a slightly open mouth showing a pale lower beak and scaly chin",
      "where": "at the anterior end, extended forward from the shell on a thick neck, facing to the right"
    },
    {
      "part": "neck",
      "looks_like": "short, thick and wrinkled, covered in large rounded overlapping scales",
      "where": "connecting the head to the anterior opening of the shell"
    },
    {
      "part": "shell",
      "looks_like": "high-domed carapace with a hard rim of large light-tan scutes showing dark growth bands and radiating lines; the dorsal two-thirds is completely obscured by dense fur, while the ventral and marginal scutes are exposed",
      "where": "occupying the entire dorsal mid-body from just behind the neck to above the hind legs"
    },
    {
      "part": "mane",
      "looks_like": "dense, long, shaggy, coarse fur in mixed dark and light brown, with individual strands visible, draping over the top and sides of the shell and extending slightly over the upper hind leg",
      "where": "covering the dorsal surface of the shell from the anterior edge behind the neck to the posterior edge above the tail"
    },
    {
      "part": "legs",
      "looks_like": "four massive, columnar, elephantine legs covered in small pebbly scales with larger pointed conical tubercles on the anterior faces of the forelegs; skin is wrinkled at the joints",
      "where": "two forelegs under the anterior shell and two hindlegs under the posterior shell, supporting the body above the ground"
    },
    {
      "part": "feet",
      "looks_like": "broad, stumpy, heavily scaled feet with short blunt nails/claws, three to four visible on each foot, with thick rounded toes",
      "where": "at the distal ends of each of the four legs, in contact with the ground"
    },
    {
      "part": "tail",
      "looks_like": "short, conical and pointed, covered in small hexagonal scales tapering to a tip",
      "where": "protruding posteriorly from under the rear rim of the shell, above the hind legs, on the left side of the image"
    },
    {
      "part": "plates",
      "looks_like": "large, hard, polygonal scutes with layered edges and concentric patterning in tan, cream and dark brown",
      "where": "forming the exposed ventral and marginal rim of the shell around the sides, front and rear, and the plastron edge visible between the forelegs"
    },
    {
      "part": "scales",
      "looks_like": "small to large, dry, polygonal and pebbly reptilian scales in tan and brown, larger and more plate-like on the head and neck, smaller and more granular on the limbs, with enlarged spiky tubercles on the forelegs",
      "where": "covering the head, neck, all four legs, feet, and tail, and the skin around the shell openings"
    }
  ],
  "attached_objects": [],
  "animals": [
    "tortoise"
  ],
  "separate_bodies": 1,
  "heads": 1,
  "walking_legs": 4,
  "wings": 0,
  "extra_limb_pieces": 0,
  "tails": 1
}
